The resulting atom types and bond orders were used to simulate the structures of several HKUST-1 and DMOF-1 representatives, and of the $\mathsf{N i}_{2}(\mathsf{b d c})_{2}(\mathsf{d a b c o})$ MOF (see Section 3.6).
## 3.5 MFU-4 type SBU
The recently emerged family of MFU-4 frameworks40 is attractive for its selective gas sorption properties.73 The SBU of MFU-4, known also as “Kuratowski-type SBU”,74 contains $Z\mathsf{n}^{\prime\prime}\mathsf{a n d}/\mathsf{o r}\mathsf{C o}^{\prime\prime}$ centers with different coordination. The central metal site has octahedral configuration and is coordinated to six triazolate ligands, which in turn connect four tetrahedrally coordinated metal sites. The tetrahedral coordination environment of the latter is fulfilled by a capping chlorine ligand, see Fig. 5.
Considering the specificity of this SBU, and in order to avoid over-parameterization, we employed the following combination of atom types to describe the cluster: Zn3f2 (as parameterized for the $Z n_{4}O$ SBU) to describe the tetrahedral $Z n^{11}$ ions, $Z n_{\mathrm{tet}},$ and $Z n4+2$ and $\cos4+2$ (as parameterized for the respective Zn- and Co-containing paddlewheel SBUs) to describe the octahedral $Z n^{11}$ and ${\mathsf{C o}}^{\parallel}$ central sites, $Z n_{\mathrm{oct}}$ and $\mathsf{C o}_{\mathsf{o c t}}$ . For the tetrahedrally coordinated ${\mathsf{C o}}^{\parallel}$ ions, $\mathsf{C o}_{\mathsf{t e t}},$ a new atom type $\cos+2$ , with $r_{i}=1.24\textup{\AA},\vartheta_{0}=109.47^{\circ}$ and coordination number $=4$ (Table 1), was introduced in view of the experimental geometry of MFU-4(Co) and MFU- $V(\mathsf{C o_{4}Z n})$ .40b For the light elements, we used the standard UFF atom types C_R, N_R, Cl and ${\sf H}_{-}$ . Bonds were described using bond orders of $\%$ for $M_{\mathrm{td}}\mathrm{-}{\mathsf{N}},$ , 1 for $N_{\mathrm{tet}}{-}C|$ , $M_{\mathrm{oct}}\mathrm{-}\mathsf{N}$ and $C-H_{\mathrm{,}}$ , and 1½ for the remaining resonant bonds (see Fig. 5a).
The UFF performance is illustrated in Table 7 for selected bond lengths and angles of the SBU of MFU-4l $(\mathsf{C o_{4}Z n})$ . Obviously, the agreement with the experimental benchmark is excellent for the $\mathsf{C o}_{\mathsf{t e t}}\mathrm{-}\mathsf{N}$ and $\mathsf{C o}_{\mathsf{t e t}}\mathrm{-}\mathsf{C l}$ bond lengths, as well as for the $\mathsf{N{-}}\mathsf{Z}\mathsf{n}_{\mathsf{o c t}}{-}\mathsf{N}$ bond angle. The largest deviation is obtained for the angles characterizing the $\mathsf{C o}_{\mathsf{t e t}}$ centers, $N{\mathrm{-}}C0_{\mathrm{{tet}}}{\mathrm{-}}N$ and $N{\mathrm{-}}C0_{\mathrm{{tet}}}{\mathrm{-}}C|$ , and yet the calculated errors are below
